    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a760ce15-da79-5d83-993a-2c64a2bdde17",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\pi.$\n- **II.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+2n\\pi.$\n- **III.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=\\pi+2n\\pi.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186176047/assets/cosine.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi$. Every zero must be included.\n\n- Statement II is false. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\n\n- Statement III is true. The minimum value is $-1$, attained at $x=\\pi+2n\\pi$. Every minimum input must be included.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e0af2665-e491-5ac1-b3d7-68f9f114422d",
